      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/united-states/napaskiak"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Napaskiak’s name has shifted over time: from “Napaskeagamiut” in 1890 to “Napaiskak” in 1950–60, before settling on its current spelling in 1970.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napaskiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village was formally incorporated in 1971, giving it official city status within the Yukon-Kuskokwim Delta region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napaskiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Napaskiak sits at 60°42′25″N 161°45′39″W, placing it deep in Alaska’s western interior along the Kuskokwim River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napaskiak%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Yup'ik people have inhabited the Napaskiak area for countless generations, and their subsistence traditions still shape village life today.",
